  <prompt>Change `Spaarke.FieldMapping.Push.pushUpdates` in `sprk_fieldmapping_push.js` so the Matter and Project "Push Updates" button opens a code-page dialog (`Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo`, pageType webresource) that hosts `RecordFamilyModal` for the current record, instead of pushing directly. Create the minimal code page that hosts the modal.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE front-end developer, Dataverse ribbon web resources and React code pages.</role>
  <goal>The button opens the Family view; no push happens unless the person confirms rows in the modal (after 040, through the modal's actions).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-35 (owner: keep the button; it opens the Family view). Today pushUpdates → openConfirmDialog → POST /push for every target profile (sprk_fieldmapping_push.js ~:423-484). The enable rule `hasSourceProfile` stays. The ribbon RibbonDiff entries (sprk_Matter/RibbonDiff.xml ~:231, ~:455; sprk_Project) keep the same command and library — only the function body changes, so no ribbon XML change is expected.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/client/webresources/js/sprk_fieldmapping_push.js</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/webresources/js/sprk_wizard_commands.js (~:156 navigateTo dialog pattern)</file>
      <file role="new">src/solutions/RecordFamily/ (minimal code page: src/main.tsx rendering RecordFamilyModal from the dialog data (entity, id))</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">an existing small code page under src/solutions/ for the build/auth bootstrap (choose the smallest; name it in the notes)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">docs/architecture/SPAARKE-SIDE-PANE-NAVIGATION.md (code-page build step; record whether ensureNavigatorSidePane applies to a dialog-only page)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-35">No direct /push call remains in pushUpdates; the old confirm dialog path is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050">Ribbon → code-page dialog is the sanctioned launch for a modal from a non-React surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 tokens; dark-mode safe.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §12">Node install in src/solutions/*: `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Deployment is task 076 (code-page-deploy / dataverse-deploy skills).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/standards/MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/SPAARKE-SIDE-PANE-NAVIGATION.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
